# Away: harness starts it as away mode comes on (everyone out for
# [butler] away_after, a trip under way, or /away): one line saying so,
# and one tap before the heating goes down. While you're away, doors,
# windows and movement come at once (triggers.ini's away-... sections),
# the lights rules lets harness:away switch go on and off in the
# evening, and one line comes at 20:00; before you're back the heating
# goes up again. Nothing guarded is ever touched.
workflow away
subject house
about When the house is empty (everyone out <away after>, a trip, or /away): a line, and one tap before the heating goes down.
start owner, harness:away
tag no
limits steps 10, days 1
#if thermostat

step warm
tool home/home_wait {"device": "<thermostat>", "property": "setpoint", "condition": ">", "value": "<away temp>", "timeout_s": 0}
on fail goto tell
if warm has not within goto tell

step ask
approve {input} Heating to <away temp> °C while you're away?
yes Heating to <away temp> °C
no Leave it
timeout 12h
on deny goto quiet

step heat
tool home/home_set {"device": "<thermostat>", "action": "temperature", "value": "<away temp>"}
on fail goto heat_failed
if heat starts done goto heat_done

step heat_unsure
say I set the heating to <away temp> °C, but the <thermostat label> hasn't confirmed: {heat}
end

step heat_done
say Heating is set to <away temp> °C.
end

step heat_failed
say The heating didn't change: {heat.error}
end

step quiet
end
#end

step tell
say {input}
